# Chroma library, modern Earth: THE WORLD ANSWERS, writer 4 (F3 rivals, allies and the successor; spec
# chroma-world/spheres/world-answers-v1.md section 6, 10-19). Read only with the Engine's world_answers switch on
# (sub-switch wa_phase2): a Known life meets named figures in the sphere where it is Known.
#   rival_push      3   a rival at rung 3 or more pushes the sphere their own way; how {N} meets it
#   ally_won        2   an ally comes over
#   ally_lost       2   an ally drifts away
#   successor_seen  2   a younger one shows they could carry it on
#   successor_hand  2   the handover; the successor goes their own way (options carry hand: chosen | open | stay)
# Sphere-neutral: no sphere: line; the Engine fills {place} (their place in that sphere), {sphere_name} (the sphere's
# plain name), {rival}, {ally} and {successor}. Everyday layout: five one-colour ways and one cross cycle; per colour,
# its one-colour option plus the cross it leads = 140. Every option leaves one or two footprints (foot:) and most carry
# lever:. Syntax: header of build.py.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- rival_push

== the rival's plan for the whole sphere
tier: everyday
stages: adult mature elder
age: 25-90
calls: WB
rate: 1
tone: mixed
life: work, community
horizon: years
roles: rival, colleague, regular, elder
cast_want: rival_push
earth: someone with standing where you are known wants to take it a very different way, and has a plan ready
times: People with standing in the same field compete to set its rules, and the field moves with whoever gathers more of what it values (Bourdieu 1993)
gap: 3-8
scene: {rival} has stood high in {sphere_name} in this town for years, and has never liked the way {N} does things. This season {rival} has a plan to change how the whole of it runs, starting with {place}, and has been talking it up at every meeting that matters. People keep asking {N} what {N} thinks, as if the answer would settle it. Some of the plan is good. Some of it would undo years of {Ns} work.
scene W: There is a proper way to settle what the town's {sphere_name} becomes, and it is not whoever talks longest at the most meetings.
scene U: {N} wants to know whether the plan would actually work before deciding whether to fight it.
scene B: {rival} is after standing as much as change, and standing is something {N} knows how to trade in.
scene R: {N} feels the old heat rise; it has been a long time since anyone pushed {N} this openly.
scene G: The town's ways in {sphere_name} are older than {N} and older than {rival}, and both of them are only passing through.
- W | take the plan to the open meeting and argue it on its merits, line by line | lever: voice | v: universalism, conformity | foot: place rule.counsel | chance: 70
- U | study the plan properly, and write a reply showing where it would and would not work | lever: voice | v: achievement, self-direction | foot: means time-.06 | chance: 70
- B | gather enough backers before the meeting that the plan never reaches a vote | lever: subvert | v: power | foot: person colleague | chance: 70
- R | stand up at the next meeting and take the plan apart in front of everyone | lever: voice | v: stimulation, self-direction | foot: door made an enemy | chance: 70
- G | carry on at {place} as always, and let the plan meet the town's old habits | lever: loyalty | v: tradition, security | foot: lesson old habits outlast new plans | chance: 75
- W>U | ask for a fair trial: {rival}'s way at one place for a year, then judge | lever: voice | v: universalism, achievement | foot: door kept your word | chance: 70
- U>B | find the parts of the plan that would help {Ns} own people, and back only those | lever: loyalty | v: achievement, power | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 70
- B>R | offer {rival} a share of the credit if the plan takes in {Ns} changes | lever: lead | v: power, stimulation | foot: door made a friend | chance: 70
- R>G | gather the regulars of {place} for a night to say what they would lose | lever: voice | v: benevolence, tradition | foot: place gather.hall | chance: 70
- G>W | ask the oldest hands how such fights were settled before, and hold to that | lever: loyalty | v: tradition, conformity | foot: person elder | chance: 65
works: The plan that goes ahead carries {Ns} mark as much as {rival}'s, and people in town say so.
works: {rival} still disagrees with {N} about most things, but no longer acts as if {N} were not there.
fails: {rival}'s plan goes ahead mostly as written, and {N} watches some of {Ns} work at {place} quietly undone.
fails: The fight drags on for a year and leaves the people at {place} tired of both of them.

== the rival drawing the newcomers away
tier: everyday
stages: adult mature elder
age: 25-90
calls: UR
rate: 1
tone: mixed
life: work, community, friends
horizon: years
roles: rival, regular, colleague
cast_want: rival_push
earth: a rival across town has started something new, and the newer faces at your place keep drifting over to it
times: Members unhappy with a group can leave or speak up, and loyalty decides which; a rival offering a livelier home makes leaving easy (Hirschman 1970)
gap: 3-8
scene: Lately the newer faces at {place} keep slipping off to whatever {rival} is running across town. {rival} has always said {Ns} way is tired, and now there are numbers to show for it: fresh people, loud evenings, a name around town. Two of {Ns} own regulars went last week, just to see. Nobody has said anything out loud, but everyone in {sphere_name} is watching what {N} does next.
scene W: A place that treats everyone fairly and keeps its word does not need to chase anyone; {N} wants to believe that.
scene U: Something over there is working, and {N} would rather understand it than resent it.
scene B: People go where they get more; {N} can offer more, if {N} decides to.
scene R: {N} misses the noise of a full room, and {rival} has it.
scene G: The ones who belong at {place} know it in their bones; the rest were only visiting.
- W | keep the doors open and the rules fair, and trust people to come back | lever: loyalty | v: conformity, security | foot: lesson steady places draw people back | chance: 75
- U | go along to {rival}'s evenings and learn what draws the newcomers there | v: self-direction, achievement | foot: means time-.03 | chance: 75
- B | have a quiet word with the ones who left about what {place} could offer them instead | lever: lead | v: power, achievement | foot: person regular | chance: 70
- R | put on something louder and better at {place} than anything {rival} has managed | lever: lead | v: stimulation, hedonism | foot: means money-.06 | chance: 65
- G | let them wander; the ones who belong at {place} will be back by winter | lever: neglect | v: tradition, security | foot: means ties-.03 | chance: 70
- W>B | create a proper post at {place} for newcomers, with a real say and title | lever: lead | v: conformity, achievement | foot: person colleague | chance: 65
- U>R | work out what the newcomers want, and let them run one evening a month | lever: lead | v: self-direction, stimulation | foot: person friend | chance: 65
- B>G | offer {rival} a deal: share the newcomers between the two places and keep the peace | lever: voice | v: power, security | foot: door made a friend | chance: 70
- R>W | put on a joint evening with {rival}, open to all, and let both ways show | lever: voice | v: stimulation, universalism | foot: place gather.great | chance: 75
- G>U | ask the old regulars what kept them coming all these years, and build on that | lever: loyalty | v: tradition, benevolence | foot: place gather.circle | chance: 70
works: By the turn of the year most of the newcomers are back at {place}, and some carry {Ns} name across town with them.
works: {rival} and {N} end up with two different places that need each other, and the town is livelier for both.
fails: The newcomers stay with {rival}, and {place} feels older and quieter with every season.
fails: Whatever {N} tries looks like an answer to {rival}, and people in town start to say so.

== the rival who wants the town's backing
tier: everyday
stages: adult mature elder
age: 25-90
calls: BG
rate: 1
tone: mixed
life: work, community, money
horizon: years
roles: rival, neighbour, regular
cast_want: rival_push
earth: the town has a little money and goodwill to share out where you are known, and a rival wants all of it to go their way
times: Rivals in a field compete for the backing that lets them set its course; who is backed shapes what the field becomes (Bourdieu 1993; Coser 1956)
gap: 3-8
scene: The town has a little money and a lot of goodwill to share out in {sphere_name} this year, and {rival} wants all of it to go their way. In meetings {rival} says, politely, that {place} under {N} belongs to the past. A neighbour who sits on the committee tells {N} the vote will be close.
scene W: Whatever is shared out should be shared by a rule anyone could see and check, and {N} would say so even if {place} lost by it.
scene U: {N} has years of results to show, if anyone on the committee will look at them.
scene B: Committees are people, and people remember who helped them.
scene R: {place} is not a line in a budget to {N}; it is the people in it, and they deserve someone who will say so.
scene G: {place} stood long before any committee shared out anything, and its own people have always kept it going.
- W | ask the committee to share it by a fair formula that holds whoever leads where | lever: voice | v: universalism, conformity | foot: place rule.counsel | chance: 70
- U | bring the record: what {place} has done with everything it was ever given | lever: voice | v: achievement | foot: lesson the record speaks for itself | chance: 75
- B | make sure the committee members owe {place} a favour or two before the vote | lever: subvert | v: power | foot: person go-between | chance: 65
- R | speak at the meeting from the heart about what {place} means to the people in it | lever: voice | v: benevolence, stimulation | foot: place rule.voice | chance: 70
- G | ask nothing of the town, and keep {place} going on what its own people give | lever: exit | v: tradition, self-direction | foot: means money-.06 | chance: 75
- W>R | propose an open day where every place shows its work, and the town chooses | lever: voice | v: universalism, stimulation | foot: place gather.great | chance: 70
- U>G | write the history of {place}, so the committee sees what would be lost | lever: voice | v: tradition, achievement | foot: place learn.keeping | chance: 65
- B>W | propose a fair split in public, knowing {rival} cannot be seen to oppose fairness | lever: voice | v: power, universalism | foot: door made an enemy | chance: 75
- R>U | turn the fight into a public question: what should the town's {sphere_name} be for? | lever: voice | v: stimulation, self-direction | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 70
- G>B | have the old families of {place} put in a word with the right people | lever: loyalty | v: tradition, power | foot: person neighbour | chance: 65
works: The vote goes the way {N} hoped, and {rival} takes it with better grace than anyone expected.
works: {place} keeps what it needs, and {Ns} way stays on the table in town for years to come.
fails: The committee leans to {rival}, and {place} has a lean year to show for it.
fails: {N} wins the vote but not the room, and {rival} starts counting heads for the next one.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- ally_won

== the doubter who comes over
tier: everyday
stages: adult mature elder
age: 25-90
calls: WR
rate: 1
tone: joy
life: work, community, friends
horizon: years
roles: colleague, regular, friend
cast_want: ally_won
earth: someone who kept a polite distance for years comes to you and says they will stand with you from now on
times: People follow a leader they come to see as one of their own, and those won over late often hold the firmest (Hogg 2001)
gap: 3-8
scene: For years {ally} kept a polite distance from {N}, running things a different way across town in {sphere_name}. This month, after seeing what {N} managed at {place}, {ally} comes by and says it plainly: the next time {N} stands for something, {ally} will stand too. It is a real offer, and others will notice how {N} takes it.
scene W: {N} wants nobody's backing on special terms; what {ally} gets, anyone who comes over should get.
scene U: {ally} doubted {N} for years, and the reasons may still be worth hearing.
scene B: A respected name changing sides is worth a great deal, if it is seen.
scene R: {N} feels a rush of gladness; it is good to be believed in by someone who did not have to.
scene G: Trust between two people grows like anything else, slowly and over many seasons.
- W | welcome {ally} in on the same terms as everyone else, no special place | lever: loyalty | v: universalism, conformity | foot: person colleague | chance: 75
- U | ask {ally} what changed {ally}'s mind, and learn from the answer | v: self-direction | foot: lesson doubters see what friends miss | chance: 70
- B | give {ally} a seat at the table straight away, where others can see it | lever: lead | v: power, achievement | foot: means ties+.06 | chance: 70
- R | throw an arm round {ally} and plan something bold together that very evening | lever: lead | v: stimulation, benevolence | foot: person friend | chance: 75
- G | let it grow slowly: a shared meal, the regulars, time to see if {ally} belongs | lever: loyalty | v: tradition, security | foot: place gather.house | chance: 75
- W>G | write down together what the two places owe each other, in plain words | lever: loyalty | v: conformity, tradition | foot: door kept your word | chance: 65
- U>W | work out with {ally} which way works better, and agree to go by it | lever: voice | v: achievement, universalism | foot: means time-.03 | chance: 70
- B>U | have {ally} train the newest people at {place}, and see what {ally} knows | lever: lead | v: achievement, power | foot: person regular | chance: 70
- R>B | take {ally} to the next big meeting, so the town sees them together | lever: voice | v: stimulation, power | foot: place rule.voice | chance: 65
- G>R | bring {ally}'s people and {Ns} people together for a night of food and old songs | lever: loyalty | v: tradition, hedonism | foot: place gather.hall | chance: 65
works: Within a year people in town speak of {ally} and {N} in the same breath, and things that stalled for years begin to move.
works: {ally} turns out to be the one who can say what {N} cannot, and says it well.
fails: Some of {Ns} old regulars never quite trust {ally}, and mutter about turncoats.
fails: {ally} comes over in name, but keeps to the old ways when it counts.

== the old opponent after a hard year
tier: everyday
stages: adult mature elder
age: 25-90
calls: UG
rate: 1
tone: mixed
life: work, community
horizon: years
roles: colleague, regular, elder
cast_want: ally_won
earth: someone who argued against you at every meeting has had a hard year, and asks to work with you from now on
times: Old opponents who share a hard time often become firm allies; conflict can bind as well as divide (Coser 1956)
gap: 3-8
scene: {ally} once argued against {N} at every meeting in {sphere_name}. Now {ally}'s own place has had a hard year, and {ally} turns up at {place} with an awkward smile and a question: could they work together from now on? A few of {Ns} people remember the old arguments very well.
scene W: Old quarrels closed fairly stay closed; {N} has always believed that, and now it is tested.
scene U: Before promising anything, {N} would like to know what went wrong over there.
scene B: {ally} needs {N} more than {N} needs {ally}, and both of them know it.
scene R: It is hard to stay cross with someone who has come to the door like this.
scene G: The people of {place} have taken in strays before, and most of them stayed.
- W | agree, and tell everyone at {place} plainly that the old arguments are closed | lever: loyalty | v: universalism, benevolence | foot: door kept your word | chance: 70
- U | look into what went wrong at {ally}'s place before promising anything | v: achievement, security | foot: means time-.03 | chance: 75
- B | agree, on terms that leave {place} the stronger partner | lever: lead | v: power, security | foot: person colleague | chance: 70
- R | laugh about the old fights over a drink, and start again from tonight | lever: loyalty | v: hedonism, benevolence | foot: person friend | chance: 75
- G | take {ally} in as one of {place}'s own, the way the place always has | lever: loyalty | v: tradition, benevolence | foot: place gather.circle | chance: 70
- W>U | set up a shared meeting where both places solve their problems in the open | lever: found | v: universalism, achievement | foot: place rule.counsel | chance: 70
- U>B | learn what {ally}'s place does well, and use it to grow {place} | lever: lead | v: achievement, power | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 65
- B>R | let {ally} take the lead on one bold project, with {Ns} name behind it | lever: lead | v: power, stimulation | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 70
- R>G | throw a joint feast for both places, so the regulars can make their own peace | lever: loyalty | v: hedonism, tradition | foot: place gather.great | chance: 65
- G>W | ask the old hands at {place} to agree first, then shake on it before them | lever: loyalty | v: tradition, conformity | foot: person elder | chance: 70
works: {ally} turns out to be a better friend than an opponent ever was, and both places come out of the hard year stronger.
works: The old arguments become a joke at {place}, told about {ally} and {N} alike.
fails: The old quarrel comes back at the first real disagreement, and both of them feel foolish.
fails: Some of {Ns} people never forgive {ally}, and the work stays split in two.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- ally_lost

== the ally sitting beside the rival
tier: everyday
stages: adult mature elder
age: 25-90
calls: BR
rate: 1
tone: trouble
life: work, community, friends
horizon: years
roles: rival, colleague, friend, elder
cast_want: ally_lost
earth: someone who has stood with you for years has started sitting beside your rival, and everyone has noticed
times: Allies drift when another side offers more or asks less; trust and closeness decide how far (Hirschman 1970; Granovetter 1973)
gap: 3-8
scene: {ally} has stood with {N} in {sphere_name} for years, at the meetings and at {place}. Lately {ally} misses the evenings that matter, and last week sat beside {rival} and nodded along. Nobody has said a word about it to {N}, which is how {N} knows that everyone has noticed.
scene W: {N} would rather have a plain answer than a slow fade; whatever {ally} decides, {ally} owes {N} that.
scene U: {rival} offered something, or {N} stopped offering something; either way, {N} wants to know which.
scene B: Loyalty has a price like anything else, and {N} can afford to pay it.
scene R: It stings, and {N} is not good at pretending it does not.
scene G: People drift and come back over a long life; holding too hard only pushes them further.
- W | ask {ally} straight out where {ally} stands, and accept the answer | lever: voice | v: conformity, universalism | foot: lesson a plain question saves months | chance: 70
- U | find out quietly what {rival} offered that {N} did not | v: achievement | foot: person go-between | chance: 70
- B | make {ally} a better offer than {rival} can | lever: lead | v: power | foot: means money-.06 | chance: 70
- R | go round to {ally}'s door that night and have it out, loudly if need be | lever: voice | v: stimulation, self-direction | foot: person friend lost | chance: 70
- G | let {ally} go without a word; people find their way back, or they do not | lever: neglect | v: tradition, security | foot: means ties-.03 | chance: 80
- W>B | thank {ally} in public for the years together, and fill the gap {ally} leaves fairly | lever: lead | v: conformity, achievement | foot: person colleague | chance: 70
- U>R | work out what {ally} wanted that {place} never gave, and change it for the next ones | lever: lead | v: self-direction, stimulation | foot: means time-.03 | chance: 70
- B>G | keep {ally} close with small kindnesses, so the door never quite shuts | lever: loyalty | v: power, benevolence | foot: door made a friend | chance: 70
- R>W | wish {ally} well at the next meeting, in front of everyone, and mean it | lever: voice | v: benevolence, universalism | foot: place rule.counsel | chance: 70
- G>U | ask the old hands at {place} what {ally} said to them, and listen | lever: loyalty | v: tradition, benevolence | foot: person elder | chance: 60
works: {ally} does not come back, but the two of them part well, and {ally} still speaks warmly of {N} around town.
works: A year on, {ally} drifts back to {place}, a little sheepish, and is welcomed.
fails: {ally} ends up firmly at {rival}'s side, and takes two of {Ns} people along.
fails: The parting turns sour, and both of them say things around town that they later regret.

== the ally who cannot back this one
tier: everyday
stages: adult mature elder
age: 25-90
calls: WG
rate: 1
tone: mixed
life: work, community, friends
horizon: years
roles: colleague, friend, neighbour, elder
cast_want: ally_lost
earth: someone who has backed you through every argument says that on your latest decision, they cannot stand with you
times: Ties between allies weaken when one decision costs the other too much; the tie holds where trust is old and deep (Granovetter 1973)
gap: 3-8
scene: {ally} has backed {N} through every argument in {sphere_name} for years. But {Ns} last decision at {place} sat badly with {ally}, and now {ally} has said so, quietly but firmly: from here on, {ally} will not stand with {N} on this. It is not a quarrel yet. It could become one.
scene W: The decision was made properly, and {N} owes it to everyone to stand by it, even now.
scene U: If {ally} sees a flaw, it is worth one more hard look; {ally} is rarely wrong for no reason.
scene B: Backing is worth something, and {N} has just lost some; it can be found elsewhere.
scene R: This is not about the decision for {N}; it is about a friend stepping back.
scene G: Old ties bend before they break, and this one has bent before.
- W | hold to the decision, since it was made fairly, and tell {ally} so with respect | lever: loyalty | v: conformity, universalism | foot: door kept your word | chance: 70
- U | go over the decision again with {ally}, point by point, to see who has missed what | lever: voice | v: self-direction, achievement | foot: means time-.03 | chance: 70
- B | let {ally} go, and win over someone with more standing to fill the gap | lever: lead | v: power, achievement | foot: person colleague | chance: 70
- R | tell {ally} how much this hurts, and hope the friendship holds where the agreement does not | lever: voice | v: benevolence | foot: lesson saying it aloud helps | chance: 70
- G | let the decision soften with time, and keep {ally} at the table for the old friendship | lever: loyalty | v: tradition, benevolence | foot: place gather.circle | chance: 75
- W>R | put the decision to an open vote at {place}, so {ally}'s doubt gets a fair hearing | lever: voice | v: universalism, self-direction | foot: place rule.counsel | chance: 70
- U>G | ask the people it touched how it has gone, and let that settle it | lever: voice | v: benevolence, tradition | foot: person neighbour | chance: 70
- B>W | offer {ally} the lead on putting the decision right, if {ally} thinks it wrong | lever: lead | v: power, universalism | foot: door made a friend | chance: 70
- R>U | admit the doubt aloud, and ask {ally} to help find a better way | lever: voice | v: stimulation, self-direction | foot: door owned up | chance: 70
- G>B | keep close to {ally}'s family, and trust the old ties to pull {ally} back | lever: loyalty | v: tradition, security | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 65
works: {ally} stays out of this one matter, and the two of them go on standing together on everything else.
works: The argument clears the air, and {ally} comes back to {Ns} side more firmly than before.
fails: {ally} drifts further off with every meeting, and by the year's end they nod politely at each other and little more.
fails: Others in {sphere_name} notice that {ally} has stepped back, and start to wonder what {ally} knows.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- successor_seen

== the week the younger one held it together
tier: everyday
stages: adult mature elder
age: 30-90
calls: UG
rate: 1
tone: joy
life: work, community
horizon: years
roles: colleague, regular, elder
cast_want: successor_seen
earth: while you were away, a younger one at your place handled a real problem, in a way you never would have
times: In midlife many turn to guiding the next generation, and seeing a younger one rise is part of that turn (Erikson 1950; Kram 1985)
gap: 3-8
scene: While {N} was away for a week, something went wrong at {place}, and {successor} sorted it out before anyone thought to call {N}. {successor} is younger, a regular for a few years now, and does things in a way {N} never would. When {N} comes back, several people make a point of telling {N} about it.
scene W: Good work done for the place deserves to be seen and given its due, whoever did it.
scene U: {N} wants to know exactly what {successor} did, and why it worked.
scene B: A rising one remembers who opened the first doors, and {N} has doors to open.
scene R: {N} feels a surprising glow of pride, as if the win were partly {Ns} own.
scene G: Places like {place} carry on because someone younger is always quietly learning to hold them.
- W | thank {successor} in front of everyone, and give {successor} a proper part in running things | lever: lead | v: conformity, benevolence | foot: person colleague | chance: 70
- U | sit down with {successor} and go through exactly what {successor} did and why | lever: lead | v: self-direction, achievement | foot: lesson the young see it differently | chance: 75
- B | keep {successor} close, and make sure {successor} knows who opened the doors | lever: lead | v: power | foot: door made a friend | chance: 70
- R | tell {successor} it was brilliant, and hand over the next big thing to run | lever: lead | v: stimulation, benevolence | foot: means time+.03 | chance: 70
- G | say little, and watch how {successor} carries it over the coming seasons | lever: loyalty | v: tradition, security | foot: lesson time shows who is ready | chance: 75
- W>G | teach {successor} the old ways of {place}, one season at a time | lever: loyalty | v: tradition, conformity | foot: door kept your word | chance: 70
- U>W | write down how {place} really runs, so {successor} or anyone could carry it on | lever: lead | v: universalism, achievement | foot: place learn.keeping | chance: 65
- B>U | send {successor} to train with the best in {sphere_name}, at {Ns} own cost | lever: fund | v: power, achievement | foot: means money-.06 | chance: 70
- R>B | introduce {successor} to everyone who matters in town, with a word of praise for each meeting | lever: lead | v: stimulation, power | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 70
- G>R | bring {successor} to the big yearly gathering to meet everyone | lever: loyalty | v: tradition, stimulation | foot: place gather.great | chance: 65
works: Over the next year {successor} grows into the work, and people at {place} begin to picture who comes after {N}.
works: {successor} starts bringing small problems to {N}, and big ideas, and {N} looks forward to both.
fails: {successor} takes the praise as a sign the post is already theirs, and some of the old hands bristle.
fails: The next problem is harder, {successor} stumbles, and {N} wonders whether it was luck after all.

== the younger one who says it better
tier: everyday
stages: adult mature elder
age: 30-90
calls: WB
rate: 1
tone: mixed
life: work, community
horizon: years
roles: colleague, regular, elder
cast_want: successor_seen
earth: at a meeting, a younger one stands up and says the way you have always done something is wrong, and is mostly right
times: A protege's growth often begins with open disagreement, and a mentor's answer shapes whether it becomes rivalry or trust (Kram 1985)
gap: 3-8
scene: At the monthly meeting at {place}, {successor}, one of the younger ones, stands up and says the way {N} has always done a certain thing is wrong. The room goes quiet. The worst of it is that {successor} is mostly right, and says it better than {N} could have at that age.
scene W: If the young one is right, the fair thing is to say so, here, in front of the people who heard it.
scene U: Mostly right is not right; {N} wants to see the working before anything changes.
scene B: {successor} has just shown the room a kind of nerve that will go far, and {N} can either ride it or stand in its way.
scene R: {N} remembers being that age, that sure, and that loud, and cannot help smiling.
scene G: The old way has kept {place} going for a long time, and that counts for something too.
- W | agree in front of the room, and change the practice as {successor} proposed | lever: lead | v: universalism, conformity | foot: door owned up | chance: 65
