- U | go and see, for a few weeks, how the new way works before saying anything | hand: chosen | v: self-direction | foot: means time-.03 | chance: 70
- B | let it be known around town that {N} could come back, and wait to be asked | hand: stay | lever: subvert | v: power | foot: door made an enemy | chance: 70
- R | go straight to {successor}, say what is wrong, and leave it there | hand: chosen | lever: voice | v: self-direction, stimulation | foot: lesson say it once, then let go | chance: 70
- G | find somewhere new for the old regulars to meet, the way it used to be | hand: open | lever: found | v: tradition, benevolence | foot: place gather.circle | chance: 70
- W>R | call an open meeting where the regulars and {successor} can have it out fairly | hand: open | lever: voice | v: universalism, stimulation | foot: place rule.counsel | chance: 65
- U>G | write down the old ways of {place}, so whatever is lost can be found again | hand: chosen | lever: loyalty | v: tradition, achievement | foot: place learn.keeping | chance: 70
- B>W | use {Ns} standing to get the members a vote on {successor}'s biggest changes | hand: open | lever: voice | v: power, universalism | foot: person rival | chance: 70
- R>U | invite {successor} for a long evening, and ask what {successor} sees that {N} missed | hand: chosen | lever: loyalty | v: stimulation, self-direction | foot: person friend | chance: 70
- G>B | stand with the old regulars, quietly, and let {successor} feel how many they are | hand: stay | lever: loyalty | v: tradition, power | foot: person regular | chance: 70
works: In time {successor}'s way settles in, and even the old regulars admit some of it is better.
works: {N} and {successor} find a way to talk about {place} that leaves them both standing.
fails: The old regulars and the new ones stop speaking, and {N} is blamed on both sides.
fails: {successor} hears what {N} did and takes it as a going back on the handover.
